    6	peak, a band of O(N^{0.42}) "spike" eigenvalues absent from the matched
    7	random baseline, and an MP bulk at rate c = phi(W)/W.
    8	
    9	The spike COUNT is empirically polynomial; the next question is what the
    10	spike EIGENVECTORS encode arithmetically. Three candidate origins:
    11	  (a) Residue-class biases pi(N; q, a) for small q;
    12	  (b) Selberg / explicit-formula low-lying zeta-zero contributions;
    13	  (c) Cross-block correlation modes (i.e., pure linear-algebraic noise).
