he second-moment of pi(N; q, a) over residue classes (Gallagher 1970, Montgomery-Vaughan MNT I Ch.17), so the C2 spectral barrier reduces to the Gallagher 2nd-moment — a quantity itself controlled by Bombieri-Vinogradov/PNT-in-AP, with no polylog method. (d) Closes the "look-up L(1, chi) to compute pi(N) via spectral compression" route hoped for by S82. **Closure mode C** (circular): to compute `sum_block sigma^2` one would need pi(N; p, *) for small p, which is itself the PNT-in-AP problem. Cites E2.1, E1.5, S74, S82. Cross-domain refs: Gallagher 1970 *Mathematika 23*; Montgomery-Vaughan 2007 *MNT I* Ch.17; Davenport 2000 *MNT* Ch.6 (closed-form L(1, chi) via digamma). See experiments/constructions/spike_eigenvalue_l_squared/. | 148 |
