    767	| C4 (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — Aggarwal × Dusart × BPSW unified p_n library | REFINEMENT | E | Composition of E6.6 (Aggarwal binary search optimality) + E6.8 (Dusart bracket of width n) + E5.1 (BPSW as TC^0 primality oracle). Built three modes: `agg` (Aggarwal binary search on `pi_lucy(x)`, no BPSW), `bpsw` (BPSW-walk from 2, no Dusart), `hybrid` (Aggarwal narrow-to-K then BPSW-walk in `[L, R]`). All three agree with `sympy.prime(n)` at n ∈ {1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 10, 25, 50, 100, 168, 169, 500, 1000, 10⁴, 10⁵, 10⁶, 10⁷}. Wall-clock benchmark @ pure-Python `pi_lucy`: at n = 10⁶ agg = 379 ms, bpsw = 15.27 s, hybrid (K=64) = 291 ms. **F1 (agreement) HOLDS**; **F3 (hybrid ≥ 10× bpsw at n ≥ 10⁴) HOLDS** at 21×/34×/53× across n ∈ {10⁴, 10⁵, 10⁶}; **F2 (hybrid ≥ 1.5× agg at n ≥ 10⁵) PARTIALLY FAILS** in pure-Python regime (only 1.30× at n = 10⁶) but HOLDS at 1.64× when `pi_lucy` is C-accelerated; **F4 (U-shape in K) FAILS** in pure-Python regime — the K-sweep at n = 10⁶ is monotone-decreasing in time, optimum is K = bracket-width (composition collapses to E6.8 + E5.1 with no Aggarwal narrowing); **F4 HOLDS** under C-accelerated `pi_lucy`: K-sweep at n = 10⁷ shows U-shape with K* ≈ 16384 ≈ √(bracket width), inflating to 0.49 s at K = bracket width. **Net new content**: (a) **the optimal K depends on the `pi(x) / BPSW` cost ratio**, a knob invisible at asymptotic-order analysis (Aggarwal 2025) — Python `pi_lucy` regime: K* = width; C-Lucy: K* ≈ √width; HKM/primecount projection: K* ≈ small constant ⇒ Aggarwal-pure dominates, BPSW adds nothing; (b) **BPSW conditionality propagates 1-to-1 through Aggarwal's wrapper**, not amplified — a single BPSW pseudoprime in the final `[L, R]` shifts the answer by exactly one prime; (c) the **Dusart bracket alone is worth ~50× over naive BPSW-from-2**, matching predicted `2 p_n / n ~ 2 log p_n` at n = 10⁴-10⁷. **Closure mode E** (equivalence): hybrid is a constant-factor re-arrangement of Aggarwal's `O(sqrt(n) log⁴ n)` bound, not an asymptotic improvement; the BPSW conditional is the only non-trivial composition content. No polylog opening — the bottleneck remains `pi(x)` evaluation at HKM/Lucy cost. Cites E5.1, E6.6, E6.8 (annotated). Cross-domain ingredient: none (all three components were already in the project's catalogue). See `algorithms/aggarwal_dusart_bpsw/`. | 120 |
    768	| C7 (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — calibrated 1-bit-bias random control for the S84 PRIMES-vs-random depth-2 sign-threshold gap | REFINEMENT | C | Composition of E1.10 / E3.13 (35-measure pseudorandomness battery, `novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md`) + S84 result (PRIMES min M=6 vs unbiased matched-density random min M ∈ {7,8} at N=6, binomial p < 0.001). S84 conjectured the gap was driven by PRIMES's 1-bit-predictor advantage (bit_0 = "is x odd" gives 75.0% accuracy on PRIMES at N=6, vs ~66% for unbiased random of weight 18/64). C7 builds the matched-class-conditional random control `f_cal` on {0..63}: P(f_cal=1 \| x odd) = 17/32 (exactly matching PRIMES's 17 odd primes); P(f_cal=1 \| x even) = 1/32 (exactly matching PRIMES's 1 even prime, namely 2). Two modes: STRATIFIED (exact 17 odd + 1 even, weight always 18, bit_0_acc always 0.75) and BERNOULLI (independent draws; variable weight, variable bit_0_acc 0.625-0.81). 20 samples each through S84's `enum_d2_smart` ILP harness (K=1458 W=1 candidates, CBC, 120s/cell). **Pre-stated falsifiers (4 outcomes)**: F1 (≥1 stratified > 6 → residual structure), F2 (all stratified ≤ 6 → gap is oddness), F3 (≥1 stratified < 6 → calibration overshoots), F4 (stratified mean < unbiased mean → bit_0 primary driver). **Result: F2 + F3 + F4 HOLD; F1 FAILS.** Stratified histogram = {5: 4, 6: 16}, mean 5.80, max 6 — 0/20 above PRIMES; 4/20 *strictly easier* than PRIMES at M=5. Bernoulli histogram = {5: 7, 6: 11, 7: 2} — both M=7 cases have bit_0_acc < 0.75 (PRIMES's value: 0.7344 and 0.7188), empirically confirming the proposed monotonic relationship `bit_0_acc ↑ ⇒ min_M ↓` at fixed weight. PRIMES sits at +0.5σ of the calibrated distribution; under the calibrated null `P(M ≤ 6) = 1.0` (vs unbiased null `P(M ≤ 6) = 0/10 → 0.5^10 ≈ 0.001`). **The S84 PRIMES-vs-random gap REDUCES TO elementary parity** ("π(x) ≈ 1 iff x odd, for x > 2"); no PRIMES-specific structure beyond oddness. **Sub-finding** (Bernoulli stratified by bit_0_acc bins): bit_0_acc ≥ 0.78 → mean min_M = 5.50; [0.75, 0.78) → 5.67; [0.72, 0.75) → 6.40 (the M=7 region); < 0.72 → 5.00 (low-weight compensation). The (bit_0_acc, weight, min_M) surface is the structural explanation. **Closure mode C** (circular): the depth-2 gap is fully captured by an elementary fact already in the project's frame (bit_0 "free first gate" mechanism, S84 §"Mechanism: single-bit predictor advantage"); calibration formally verifies the explanation. Recommends footnote on `novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md`: 36th measure (depth-2 sign-threshold) DEVIATES from unbiased random but the deviation is fully captured by the trivial 1-bit oddness fact; pseudorandomness thesis stands "modulo the obvious mod-2 bias." **Net new content**: (a) verified S84 mechanism (bit_0 → depth-2 size) under direct calibrated control; (b) new mechanism prediction empirically confirmed (bit_0_acc-vs-min_M monotonic at fixed weight); (c) PRIMES-vs-calibrated indistinguishability removes the only known deviation in the 35+ measure battery from "structural" to "elementary parity" status. Spawned successor C7.a (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — N=8 calibrated extension. Cites E1.10, E3.13, E1.6, E1.4, S84. See experiments/circuit_complexity/sat_tc0_primes_n8_calibrated/. | 89 |
