tra heuristics** — Rédei is the GENUS-level invariant one step below the 4-rank density that C-L predicts. **Cross-domain ingredient (arithmetic topology / Mazur primes-as-knots) performed real work**: FIRST project use; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §4 row "Arithmetic topology" promoted PROPOSED → USED-E with edge E2.29. **Channelled mathematician**: Morishita (arithmetic topology) / Stevenhagen (Rédei reciprocity). **Successors proposed (S164)**: D44.a quartic Massey product `⟨p₁, p₂, p₃, p₄⟩_2` (Vogel 2004 thesis) on admissible 4-tuples — first higher-rank arithmetic-topology invariant (1-2 sessions); D44.b 4-rank distribution of `Cl(Q(√(p·q)))` (Cohen-Lenstra) on admissible (p, q) pairs (1-2 sessions); D44.c quantitative effective-Chebotarev rate test — model `|Δf_+| ∼ c / √log N` and confirm sub-5σ z-growth is finite-N effective Chebotarev for the Rédei field (1 session). Cross-domain refs: Mazur 1966 *Ann. Sci. ENS* 6, 521; Morishita 2002 *J. Reine Angew. Math.* 550, 141; Morishita 2012 *Knots and Primes* Springer; Rédei 1939 *J. Reine Angew. Math.* 180, 1; Lemmermeyer 2000 *Reciprocity Laws* CUP; Stevenhagen 1996 *Acta Arith.* 76, 89; Vogel 2004 Heidelberg PhD thesis; Wikipedia: Arithmetic topology. See `experiments/algebraic/redei_symbol_prime_triples/` and `archive/sessions/session164_d44_redei_symbol.md`. | 164 |
